WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.781 --> 00:00:03.595
- [Narrator] One afternoon in 1999,

00:00:03.595 --> 00:00:06.131
Mr. Matsumoto had an idea.

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:10.123
That idea would put his small
town of Susami on the map.

00:00:10.123 --> 00:00:13.512
(orchestral violin music)

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:16.595
(bouncy piano music)

00:00:27.973 --> 00:00:29.811
This is Mr. Matsumoto.

00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:32.561
He ran the post office in Susami.

00:00:56.392 --> 00:00:57.923
- [Narrator] In a
classic, if you build it,

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:02.090
they will come story, they
built it and people came.

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.711
- [Narrator] This is Mr. Nakanishi.

00:01:09.711 --> 00:01:11.504
He runs a dive shop here in Susami

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.754
and he manages the postbox.

00:01:25.026 --> 00:01:26.596
- [Narrator] Since the box is underwater,

00:01:26.596 --> 00:01:29.219
you can't just mail a typical postcard.

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:31.980
So it goes like this, you
come into Mr. Nakanishi's

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.563
dive shop, buy a
postcard, write your note.

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:48.386
- [Narrator] Gear up,
dive down, slip the note

00:01:48.386 --> 00:01:51.088
into the red mailbox
sitting on the ocean floor,

00:01:51.088 --> 00:01:54.156
and according to Mr.
Nakanishi, it will actually get

00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:55.739
to its destination.

00:02:15.822 --> 00:02:18.662
- [Narrator] Ultimately,
Mr. Matsumoto's idea worked.

00:02:18.662 --> 00:02:22.134
The mailbox made Susami
a destination for divers.

00:02:22.134 --> 00:02:24.217
It made the town special.

00:02:45.444 --> 00:02:48.027
(bell chiming)

